    description: "Given to God before he was born, he heard a voice in the night as a boy and thought it was the old priest calling.",
    contribution: "The last judge and the first great prophet, who anointed both of Israel's first two kings.",
    biography:
      "Samuel's mother Hannah was childless and prayed at Shiloh so intensely that Eli the priest assumed she was drunk. She vowed that if she were given a son she would give him back, and she did -- bringing him to the tabernacle as a small boy and visiting once a year with a coat she had made.\n\nHe was still a child when he heard a voice at night and ran to Eli three times before the old man realised what was happening and told him how to answer. The message he was given was a judgement on Eli's own household, and he had to deliver it in the morning.\n\nHe judged Israel for decades, travelling a circuit between towns. When he was old the elders asked for a king so they could be like the other nations. Samuel took it personally; God told him they had rejected him, not Samuel, and told him to warn them exactly what a king would do -- conscript their sons, take their daughters, tax their harvests -- and then to give them one anyway.\n\nHe anointed Saul, and later had to confront him for disobedience and tell him the kingdom was torn from him. Then he was sent to Bethlehem to anoint a replacement, and worked down through seven of Jesse's sons before asking whether there were any more.\n\nHis own sons were corrupt judges, which is part of why the people wanted a king -- a detail the text does not hide.",
